00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:40,880
And, you know, if I say

620
00:27:40,880 --> 00:27:41,880
I'm trying to make a profit,

621
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:45,880
they're skeptical.

622
00:27:45,880 --> 00:27:48,880
We have one professor in our econ department, Dean Carlin,

623
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:51,880
who set up a big nonprofit.

624
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:53,880
He said,

625
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:55,880
He,

626
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:58,880
I mean, we have one of our big Asian universities,

627
00:27:58,880 --> 00:28:00,880
at Yale.

628
00:28:00,880 --> 00:28:02,880
But, it's kind of rare.

629
00:28:02,880 --> 00:28:05,880
Anyway, I'm talking here today about,

630
00:28:05,880 --> 00:28:08,880
this is called, Innovations for Poverty Action.

631
00:28:08,880 --> 00:28:10,880
And just last night,

632
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:11,880
I had a door to door,

633
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:12,880
it's my surprise,

634
00:28:12,880 --> 00:28:13,880
I had a young,

635
00:28:13,880 --> 00:28:15,880
Yale freshman come by,

636
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:17,880
asking me to donate,

637
00:28:17,880 --> 00:28:19,880
here in New Haven.

638
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:21,880
There's no donations to,

639
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:23,880
I guess Yale gets donations,

640
00:28:23,880 --> 00:28:28,120
don't get donations, generally.

641
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:29,660
All right, the value of a

642
00:28:29,660 --> 00:28:31,200
share in the company is equal

643
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:32,900
to the total value of

644
00:28:32,900 --> 00:28:34,600
the company divided by the number

645
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:35,860
of shares.

646
00:28:35,860 --> 00:28:39,840
OK, so the market cap of

647
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:43,820
a company is equal to the value

648
00:28:43,820 --> 00:28:46,640
per share times the number of shares.

649
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:52,080
Market cap is short for market capitalization.

650
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:57,320
And that is the value of the company.

651
00:29:00,919 --> 00:29:05,389
So, the key thing you have

652
00:29:05,389 --> 00:29:09,860
to know about a company is, how

653
00:29:09,860 --> 00:29:11,520
many shares are there?

654
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:13,580
And how many shares do I have?

655
00:29:13,580 --> 00:29:15,080
Maybe I'm repeating myself.

656
00:29:15,080 --> 00:29:21,439
But if there's a million shares outstanding, and I own

657
00:29:21,439 --> 00:29:22,060
1,000 shares.

658
00:29:22,060 --> 00:29:26,000
Then I own 1,000th of everything the company owns.

659
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:28,700
Because I own after their debt.

660
00:29:32,540 --> 00:29:36,000
But if there's 10 million shares, and I own 1,000

661
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:40,000
shares, then I own only 1,000th.

662
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,919
You have to know the number of shares.

663
00:29:42,919 --> 00:29:44,359
The number of shares that

664
00:29:44,359 --> 00:29:45,800
you own is meaningless, unless you

665
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:48,300
know the total number of shares in the company.

666
00:29:48,300 --> 00:29:51,419
And all the different shares are treated equally.

667
00:29:51,420 --> 00:29:52,810
If they pay out any money

668
00:29:52,810 --> 00:29:54,200
to one shareholder, they've got to

669
00:29:54,200 --> 00:29:56,280
pay it out to all

670
00:29:56,280 --> 00:29:58,360
the other shareholders in proportion to

671
00:29:58,360 --> 00:30:01,540
the number of shares.

672
00:30:01,540 --> 00:30:03,940
Now, companies issue dividends.

673
00:30:08,100 --> 00:30:15,140
A dividend is paid to shareholders when the Board of

674
00:30:15,140 --> 00:30:17,100
Directors decides to do it.

675
00:30:17,100 --> 00:30:19,680
And the Board of Directors doesn't have to do it.

676
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:21,160
I'm talking now exclusively.

677
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:23,590
So, at a board meeting, they

678
00:30:23,590 --> 00:30:26,020
can say, hey, let's pay a

679
00:30:26,020 --> 00:30:26,520
dividend.

