00:33:05,220 --> 00:33:06,720
not paying it out, I want

758
00:33:06,720 --> 00:33:07,720
the money, right?

759
00:33:07,720 --> 00:33:09,720
So, I'm not going to vote for this board.

760
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:12,720
I'll put Carl Icahn on or someone else.

761
00:33:12,720 --> 00:33:13,720
Pay it out.

762
00:33:13,720 --> 00:33:14,720
And then that's what happens.

763
00:33:14,720 --> 00:33:16,720
They start paying it out.

764
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:19,220
When they pay out a

765
00:33:19,220 --> 00:33:21,720
dividend, the share price falls generally,

766
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:22,720
right?

767
00:33:22,720 --> 00:33:23,720
Very simple.

768
00:33:23,720 --> 00:33:25,720
Why would the share price fall

769
00:33:25,720 --> 00:33:27,720
when they pay out a dividend?

770
00:33:27,720 --> 00:33:29,720
Well, because the company is worth less.

771
00:33:29,720 --> 00:33:32,720
They had this money and they paid it out.

772
00:33:32,720 --> 00:33:34,220
So, it should fall by

773
00:33:34,220 --> 00:33:35,720
the amount they paid out divided

774
00:33:35,720 --> 00:33:37,720
by the number of shares, right?

775
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:39,720
And companies do that routinely.

776
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:42,720
When they declare a dividend, the price falls.

777
00:33:42,720 --> 00:33:43,720
It's called the ex-dividend.

