1430
01:00:57,900 --> 01:01:02,900
So it was one of the nifty-fifty.

1431
01:01:02,900 --> 01:01:04,900
People were very impressed with it.

1432
01:01:04,900 --> 01:01:09,900
People were very impressed with Xerox in its day.

1433
01:01:09,900 --> 01:01:12,900
So Xerox means dry in Greek.

1434
01:01:12,900 --> 01:01:15,900
It's a dry copier.

1435
01:01:15,900 --> 01:01:18,900
And it was considered a high-tech company,

1436
01:01:18,900 --> 01:01:21,900
moving forward rapidly.

1437
01:01:21,900 --> 01:01:24,900
But then it suffered a problem.

1438
01:01:24,900 --> 01:01:25,900
Do you know what the problem was?

1439
01:01:25,900 --> 01:01:29,900
It was doing really well until sometime in the 1990s,

1440
01:01:29,900 --> 01:01:31,900
when another invention came.

1441
01:01:31,900 --> 01:01:32,900
And it wasn't Xerox's.

1442
01:01:32,900 --> 01:01:34,900
It was called digital copying machines.

1443
01:01:34,900 --> 01:01:36,900
Where they would scan in,

1444
01:01:36,900 --> 01:01:38,900
the machine would have like a computer

1445
01:01:38,900 --> 01:01:40,900
